{
 "about": "Image-generated surface textures. Each sheet is one 1:1 image holding a 3x3 grid of nine textures (row by row). materials: world material ids that use the texture (the first texture listed for a material is its default; buildings pick among all of them). meters: real-world width of one tile. tint: 0 keeps the photo's colors, 1 keeps only its light and shade and takes the color of each building. roughness: base microsurface roughness. relief: bump strength in meters. crop: optional part of the cell to keep (x0, y0, x1, y1 as fractions). flatten: 0-1, how much broad lighting gradients are evened out (default .35). art: a single picture used whole (not tiled), not a surface. mirror: tile as a mirrored 2x2 (for nearly plain materials). uniform: 'x' for patterns that run the full width (each row keeps mostly its average). art: true for a picture hung whole on the walls of rooms seen through windows, 'rug' for a floor rug. 'curtain' and 'blinds' dress the windows of rooms. uses: special places (bark of tree trunks, tactile paving, curb, flat-roof, ceiling, office-floor, rug, curtain, blinds). rooms: material ids inside furnished rooms (24 floors, 43 walls, 44 tiles).",
